# Pentatonic Box 4 Lick (repertoire plan: st-pent-box-4). An original 8-bar study in A minor
# pentatonic box 4 over a one-chord Am7 groove, played twice: first at frets 12 to 15, then the
# same music in open position, an octave lower (fret 12 becomes the open string, 13 becomes 1,
# 14 becomes 2, 15 becomes 3: the strings stay the same).
# Four 2-bar phrases in call and response: phrases 1 and 3 ask (they stop on E and on G),
# phrases 2 and 4 answer (they come home to A). All 12 notes of the box are used, and nothing else.
# Fingers as the Scales screen shows the box: at fret 12, finger 1 on fret 12, finger 2 on 13,
# finger 3 on 14, finger 4 on 15; in open position, finger 1 on fret 1, 2 on fret 2, 3 on fret 3.
# The bend is in bar 7 (and bar 15): D on string 2 bent a whole step up to E, with finger 3 and
# finger 2 behind it. The next note is the real E on string 1, so you hear at once whether the
# bend reached it (in open position that E is the open string 1).
title: Pentatonic Box 4 Lick
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study in A minor pentatonic, box 4
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: minor pentatonic, box 4, call and response, lick, bend, open position
